# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto
# Store fixtures are byte-exact, never normalized: the databases, logs, frames and
# sidecars of a fixture root, and the text beside it. A test compares
# expected_reads.txt to what it builds with LF line endings, so a CRLF checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true, the Windows runners' default) would fail it.
weftdb/tests/fixtures/** -text
# The v0.1.0 compatibility fixture (X-FX): every byte of it is what the first public release
# wrote, so nothing here may be normalized on checkout either - the databases would stop
# being the release's, and `weftdb/tests/compat_v010.rs` parses expected_reads.txt with LF
# line endings on every platform.
compat/fixtures/** -text
